## Approach
 To Solve this question we make a reverse graph like if points are u and v then we make a adjacency list from v to u and also maintain a inOrder of all elements . then we travel on InOrder if any element inorder is 0 we insert that element in queue and and maintain a ans now we travel on bfs and maintain a list we insert front element in ans and the elements which are connected from front we decrease that element inOrder if inorder is 0 then insert in queue we repeat this process until queue size becomes 0 . at the end we check if ans size is equal is to n it means we take all courses so we return true otherwise return false;

## Solution
```java[]
class Solution {
    public boolean canFinish(int n, int[][] arr) {
        ArrayList<Integer> ans = new ArrayList<>();
        ArrayList<ArrayList<Integer>> adj = new ArrayList<>();
        for(int i=0;i<n;i++) adj.add(new ArrayList<>());
        int []inOrder = new int[n];
        for(int i=0;i<arr.length;i++){
            int u = arr[i][0], v = arr[i][1];
            adj.get(v).add(u);
            inOrder[u]++;
        }
        Queue<Integer> q = new LinkedList<>();
        for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
            if(inOrder[i]==0) q.add(i);
        }
        while(q.size()>0){
            int front = q.remove();
            ans.add(front);
            for(int ele:adj.get(front)){
                inOrder[ele]--;
                if(inOrder[ele]==0) q.add(ele);
            }
        }
        return (ans.size()==n);
    }
}
```

